[lease] card | # 1.008 x its rate, so ours sums 11..13 ms a replay with ~0.1..0.5 ms of node gaps.
[lease] card | kind: profile
[lease] card | question: which kernels and how much gap make our 12.2 ms Bolt decode step, and which kernels make llama.cpp's
[lease] card |   pp512 pass?
[lease] card | term: kernel ms a replay (nsys-table.py --steps over the graph launches), generate_qwen3moe --tokens <6 ids> -n
[lease] card |   64 --ctx 256 --time, graph node tracing, RTX A6000
[lease] card | unit: ms
[lease] card | predict: 11..13
[lease] card | condition: one lease (lease-hold.sh), BLOOMERY_CARD=a6000, nsys -t cuda --cuda-graph-trace=node; llama-bench -p
[lease] card |   512 -n 0 -r 1 -ngl 99 -fa on profiled in the same hold
[lease] card | decide-in: rank the fold candidates (norm+quantize, residual epilogue) and the IQ2 rows by ms a step
[lease] card | decide-below: the step is kernel-bound with no gap term: drop the node-count levers
[lease] card | decide-above: the gaps are a term: price c_node from the window wall minus the kernel sum
[lease] card: ok kind=profile (no ruler: not an ab card)
